Z||000000||jhar1987||05-03-2001||07:36 PM||||if you were with us last episode you know that my v-6 is shutting off going down the road! still got a prob. i have changed alt,bat,cables,starter,oilswitch,fuel relay,ignition mod. today while driving the radio will turn off and on like its losing power, also at the same time the gauges bounce BIG time like losing power then it will either say running or die???????????????????????????????????||||reg||1
Z||000001||thomas_l||05-03-2001||07:51 PM||||You've either got a broken fuse link with the ends just touching (probably inside the insulation) or a REALLY bad ground.||||reg||1
Z||000002||StuGood||05-03-2001||08:16 PM||||Well, this is going to sound brilliant.  You've got an intermittent (bad) connection somewhere.  Where?<P>Try:  1)Fuses falling not tight in fusebox?  Not likely, but easy to check.  2)Connections at block on RH rear wall of engine compartment (just aft of battery). <P>Perhaps the ignition switch is going bad.  Jiggle the key around and see if things turn off and on.  Just a few suggestions.   <P>||||reg||3
Z||000003||theogre||05-03-2001||11:12 PM||||Please stop opening new threads for the same problem.<P>Test the charging system anyway. just because you changed something doesn't mean the new part is good.<P>check the Thin positive wire on the battery.<BR>Check the ALL the engine bay wiring for that matter. There are a bunch of places things could be loose/bad.||||reg||1
Z||000004||kendall||05-03-2001||11:42 PM|||| I had that problem in a car once. It ended up being (after several frustating days then going to a dealer and more cash than I care to say) the key switch was just worn out. The actual problem cost around ten bucks to fix  ||||reg||1
